    "Most technicians train at FAA-approved aviation maintenance schools or avionics programs, in the military, or on the job at repair stations. Some hold an FAA Airframe and Powerplant certificate, an FCC radio license or NCATT certification. Demand comes from airlines, business aviation, helicopters, manufacturers and repair stations."
